% The shared block advances a -> b -> c, so it counts (hit) in a and b then
% stops. Runs in BOTH modes: sequential walks the OP_NINSTATE OR-chain gate;
% reactive enters each rule past the gate (rule_ip skips it) and is driven by the
% State transitions -- proving the multi-state block fires reactively too.
{cycles, 6}.
{modes, [seq, reactive]}.
{checks, [
  {final_var, "hit", 2}
]}.
